WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.610
- This is the very first
cast that I have ever worn.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.950
It was the day I was born.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.760
This is my little knee and this
is all the way to my thigh.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.050
This is how tiny my leg is.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.380
And they put this on me
to straighten my leg.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.600
My name's Marna Michele.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.030
I'm a singer-songwriter
and I have arthrogryposis.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.720
It's a muscle and joint disorder.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.880
I have stiffness in
the joints and weakness

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.620
in the muscles, or a lack of muscles.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.590
I can't walk.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.160
I am in a wheelchair
for the rest of my life

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.890
and I can't life my arms above my head.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.740
But other than that, I am relatively

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.200
capable of doing most things.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.310
I was 12 years old and I entered into

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.470
a talent contest and I decided to sing.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.380
I won the talent competition and I decided

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.960
this is what I want to do for a living.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.090
And people always ask
me why and it's because

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:45.900
of the fact that when I was on stage

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.370
I forgot that I was incapable of walking

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.710
or that I couldn't high five someone

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.490
because my arms don't go over my head.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:56.080
I was just on stage singing
a song and people were

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.210
enjoying it and singing
along with me and I was like

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.550
this is what I want to do
for the rest of my life.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.770
Since sixth grade, I pursued singing.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:08.030
I was in choir, I would
enter into competitions

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.730
outside of school, and then when I hit 16

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.630
that was when I started
auditioning for TV shows

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.450
like X Factor and American
Idol and The Voice.

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:15.949
The challenges I've come across

00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:18.820
are people not believing in me.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.650
People who ask me questions
like what is the wheelchair

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.800
going to do for you in this industry?

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:25.470
And my answer is always the same.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.390
The wheelchair will get
me on and off stage.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.820
Your question should be what
is your voice going to do.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.690
There was this one time
that I auditioned for

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.450
a singing competition on the television

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.020
and I remember going in and I sang my song

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.210
and they said to me we like
you, we like your voice,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.781
but we don't like the wheelchair
because it's an eyesore.

00:01:44.781 --> 00:01:46.660
And so I'm like sitting there.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:49.760
I'm not gonna be on your show not cause

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.630
I'm not talented, but because
my wheelchair is an eyesore.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.860
That was probably my least
favorite experience I've had.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.180
Because I definitely don't
believe that your talent

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.870
should be related to
what's attached to you.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.700
And my wheelchair is
definitely attached to me

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.930
but it's not what defines me.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.530
I'm on my way to a performance

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.660
that I'm really excited
slash nervous about.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.830
I'm performing an original
that I wrote by myself

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.530
and I really love the meaning of it

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.860
and I hope that people
love the meaning of it.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.870
And I just love being on stage and singing

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.960
and performing and
connecting with an audience

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.960
and feeling like I can
do anything in the world.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.880
I'm so excited and I hope it goes well.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.620
The song is all about being
super confident and not

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.317
giving up on your hopes and
your dreams and being strong.

00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:43.360
And I just really hope that
people in the audience connect

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.000
to this song the way that I
connected when I wrote it.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.440
And I just feel like this is
gonna be a pretty cool song.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.730
I'm gonna perform right over there.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.590
I'm so excited.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.230
I want to show that the disabled

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.730
community has bunches of talent.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.940
Just because you're different doesn't mean

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:00.454
you can't aspire to be a doctor

00:03:00.454 --> 00:03:03.160
or a veterinarian or a lawyer or a dancer.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.000
I'm not saying I can do anything,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.360
cause I really don't believe that.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.750
I can't ever walk.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.370
But the things that I
can do and the things

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.140
I believe in myself for doing,

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.710
they're definitely gonna happen.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.913
You have to believe in yourself.

00:03:14.913 --> 00:03:19.044
♪ Let the stars ♪

00:03:19.044 --> 00:03:24.044
♪ Lead you where you are going ♪

00:03:25.524 --> 00:03:29.615
♪ Let the light ♪

00:03:29.615 --> 00:03:34.615
♪ Keep the monsters at bay ♪

00:03:36.514 --> 00:03:41.514
♪ Don't let anyone take away your faith ♪

00:03:42.045 --> 00:03:47.045
♪ Don't let anyone
diminish your strength ♪

00:03:47.245 --> 00:03:52.084
♪ Bravery is in you ♪

00:03:52.084 --> 00:03:57.084
♪ There's power in your truth ♪

00:03:57.464 --> 00:04:02.396
♪ Let's fight for all you can do ♪

00:04:02.396 --> 00:04:04.104
♪ And don't give up ♪

00:04:04.104 --> 00:04:09.104
♪ Look inside your soul
and do all you can do ♪

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:17.985
♪ Can do ♪

00:04:18.136 --> 00:04:20.469
♪ Stay true ♪

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.910
People with disabilities, we have to

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.740
believe in ourselves way
more than anybody else.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.156
Because a lot of people will look at us

00:04:30.156 --> 00:04:33.890
and they will say she's
not gonna succeed at that.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.130
A lot of people will watch this

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:37.195
and think she's not gonna go anywhere.

00:04:37.195 --> 00:04:38.030
Guess what?

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:39.660
I don't care what they think.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.520
I'm gonna go places because I'm

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.180
the one that writes my own story.

00:04:44.607 --> 00:04:49.607
♪ Be true ♪

00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:51.784
♪ Be true ♪

